---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { checkedOn, disclaimer, runs, shows, venues } from "../content";
import PageHero from "@dst/ui/PageHero.astro";
---
<Layout
  prose
  title="About this site"
  description="How musical.today builds a listing: one source per fact, the seller named next to every ticket link, and nothing filled in that has not been published."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About"
    title="About this site"
    image="/covers/about.jpg"
    imageAlt="Cut-paper illustration: a proscenium arch with one curtain drawn back."
    imageKind="generated"
  >
    <p class="lede">
      Most listings sites are a search box in front of an affiliate feed. This
      one is a hand-built calendar: {runs.length} runs, {venues.length} venues,
      each read from the production's own source and stamped with the day it was
      read. {disclaimer}
    </p>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="container prose">
    <h2>How a listing gets here</h2>
    <p>
      A run is added from the production's own listing — dates, theatre, seller
      — and nothing else is invented to fill the row. Where a theatre has not
      been announced, the page says so; where nobody is selling tickets yet, it
      says that instead of pointing at a resale site. Listings were last read on
      {" "}{checkedOn}, and that date is printed on every page it applies to.
    </p>
    <h2>Every event gets the full treatment</h2>
    <p>
      The format you see on {shows[0]!.title} — a page per run, a page per
      theatre, the history, the video, the calendar file — is the standard here,
      not a one-off. An event earns it by being worth the attention; nothing
      about the format is specific to one show.
    </p>
    <h2>Links out</h2>
    <p>
      The only links out are to sellers and to venues' own sites, and every
      button says who it leads to before you press it. This site takes no
      booking, handles no payment and sets no price.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Dates move and runs are cancelled. If something here is wrong it should be
      corrected rather than argued with; this page will carry a contact route as
      soon as the site is past its first season.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose p { max-width: 68ch; }
</style>
